      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Cognitive-behavioral therapy focuses on the cognitive, affective, and behavioral components of the pain experience. Cognitive-behavioral strategies can be used to treat chronic pain and chronic intermittent pain. The strategies concentrate on emotional, behavioral, and social responses, helping patients to increase their feelings of control or feelings of self efficacy regarding control."},
